<!--Post: 13390--><!--Time: 1115189931-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13390"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, May 03, 2005 - 11:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ROCKY- are you saying you DON&#39;T like BTK? Cause it&#39;s not clear from your writings. You seem to be beating around the bush on this subject. Oh well. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m surprised none of the media has asked- or answered this question: WHY did Rader stand mute today? What is the legal strategy for this? He has a team of lawyers who should be speaking for him- one way or another. Why didn&#39;t he just plead &#34;Not Guilty&#34; himself, or thru his lawyers???<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13390-->
<!--Post: 13391--><!--Time: 1115206738-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13391"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 4:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Vic, I have read that by pleading in the arraignment, you are basically agreeing that everything was kosher up till now, in regards to court proceedings. <BR> <BR>On the other hand, if you stand mute, you can come back later and complain &#40;appeal?&#41; the previous proceedings. <BR> <BR>Someone with more knowlege feel free to correct me, as that lawyer mumbo jumbo is pretty difficult stuff.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13391-->
<!--Post: 13398--><!--Time: 1115216392-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13398"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 7:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rader certainly has lost weight and looks better than the arrest pic. With his weight loss, he more closely resembles the younger man who did the killings, allegedly. I expected him to plead &#39;not guilty&#39; on mere formality and protection of rights. No one can say his voice is familiar if he keeps his mouth shut.  There may be something inside telling him that he truly is not guilty. I think that he is clueless and may have depersonalized all this, including the murders, viewing everything as a bad movie and he cannot get out of the theatre.  &#39;After a thing like this, I go back to my regular life&#39;, to paraphrase. I presume the defense will have their own psych exam to counteract that of the prosecution. <BR> <BR>I was pleased to learn about the Hard 40 law. Sometimes death can be a better friend than life in some instances. I do not think that Rader is cognizant of all that is going on. I would love to see the psych testing results on him. I can picture his scores already. It is too bad that his father is deceased. Rader&#39;s mother and father hold the key to this twisted affair, and death and aging has probably erased the significant event that set him on his killing course. If asked about his childhood, his mother would probably rewrite history as parents often do. I would venture to say that it was his brothers who were in court and not his immediate family &#40;wife and kids&#41;. <BR> <BR>Shall we make book on whether he will testify on his own behalf? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13398-->
<!--Post: 13400--><!--Time: 1115218340-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13400"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 7:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->See. I feel that Rader is not confused...or clueless..I think this demon @&#42;&#42; knows EXACTLY what he is doing...what he did...and was aware of it at the time.  He wants to remain in complete control...he is smug...as i said on another thread...in his pics...I SWEAR I detect a sparkle in his eyes. <BR>P.S.VS - I should more than likely let Rocky speak for herself..but I KNOW she DOES NOT like DTDC - her mother&#39;s best friend was one of his victims...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
